# The end step trigger has an intervening "if an opponent lost life this turn" (CR 603.4, 119.3). Turn 1: nobody lost life, so no
# counter (the check is made before turn 3's end step resolves anything). Turn 3: the attack costs Bot2 2 life, so Bloodthief (the
# only Vampire) puts a counter on itself. Turn 5: no attack, no life lost that turn - the life lost on turn 3 does not count -
# so it stays at one counter.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Stromkirk Bloodthief
Island x16

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Stromkirk Bloodthief.Cast
[T1 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Stromkirk Bloodthief.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Stromkirk Bloodthief > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.End]
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Stromkirk Bloodthief.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
[T5 Bot1.End]
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T6 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Battlefield.Stromkirk Bloodthief.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Stromkirk Bloodthief.Power = 3
